Z||000000||SloPonti||05-03-2000||08:43 AM||||when i first hit the gas the car just stumbles on its face and then once i floor it she runs fine! i have a new motor and everything else is new-new tbi-new cap-new rotor-new msd blaster coil-i have accell 8mm plugs wires on it that are a year old and i am going to replace them tonight with new ones but they don't look bad! i need to get this fixed before this weekend or i can't go to the illinois fiero show! so someone help me out! i was wondering if the distributor is worn out! 84 fiero with new rebuilt 4 cylinder-hooker header-comp cam-holley tbi!thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bens88GT||05-03-2000||09:54 AM||||It might be your timing. My engine had the same symptoms when I bought my car, and I was using 87 octane gas. Then I found out the previous owner had advanced the timing for 93 octane. I started using 93, and it's run like a swiss watch ever since.||||reg||3
Z||000002||Oreif||05-03-2000||09:59 AM||||Most likely it's the wires. Replace them with a perfomance wire like Accel 8.8mm or the 300 blue racing ones. Your MSD ignition will wear out regular spark plug wires. You may want to check the plugs, cap and rotor too. You will need to use the Higher Quality parts with the upgraded ignition.<BR>Hope to see ya there Saturday! <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 05-03-2000).]||||reg||1
